BUG-38, fix 1: SwAnchoredObject::CheckCharRectAndTopOfLine reuses its last answer while nothing
it depends on has changed.

SwContentNotify re-checks every at-character object of a paragraph after each MakeAll of it, and
each check builds a text cursor (GetAutoPos, GetTopOfLine): in a document with thousands of
anchored objects that was 26 s of a 54 s layout (cma), and over 262 documents 762.8 M checks of
which 99.85% (char rect) and 99.99% (top of line) found the value unchanged.

The check now keeps a key: the anchor character frame's format generation, its frame and print
areas, whether it is a follow (first-line indent), its upper's frame and print areas (GetAutoPos
limits the rectangle to the upper's print area), and the anchor position (node by identity as
well as by index, and content index). While all are
unchanged, the frame and its upper are valid, and the frame has its paragraph portion or is
empty (then GetAutoPos/GetTopOfLine only read it, an empty one only its areas; otherwise they
may format it, so nothing is cached), the check returns what it would have found: the same char
rect and top of line, i.e. nothing to do.
- SwTextFrame::mnFormatGeneration changes whenever the frame's line layout or what reading it
  depends on may change: line formatting (Format_, FormatOnceMore, FormatQuick once it rebuilds
  lines), lines truncated (SwTextIter::TruncLines) or a dummy line added, SetPara/ClearPara and
  a new paragraph portion for a non-empty frame, SetEmpty, SetOffset_ and ManipOfst when the
  value changes, SetMergedPara,
  JoinFrame/SplitFrame, Prepare (except MustFit and WidowsOrphans, which only set preparation
  flags), SwClientNotify, every path of Format() that changes the frame, and a FormatEmpty() that
  changes the height. A Format() that finds the frame formatted, a FormatEmpty() that declines or
  changes nothing, a flag-only Prepare, and CalcPreps applying preparations that change no line
  leave it alone: on heavy round-trip documents those were ~98% of the checks the cache missed
  (Prepare(MustFit) then CalcPreps alone 92 M on 16 documents), every one of which recomputed to
  the cached value. Values come from ONE global counter, so a frame
  allocated at a freed frame's address never starts at a value an old key holds.
- Every writer of the cached values (AddLastCharY, ResetLastCharRectHeight, AddLastTopOfLineY,
  ClearCharRectAndTopOfLine, sw_HideObj) clears the key.
- One answer per anchor character frame: after a frame is formatted, every object anchored
  there asks GetAutoPos/GetTopOfLine the same question of the same frame (round-trip documents
  anchor thousands of objects in textless paragraphs that are formatted on every pass). The last
  answer of each lookup is kept under the same key and in the same states, and reused by the
  other objects (cma 67.6 -> 42.8 s; three documents that never finished now do).
Not WASM-specific. Documents module only for now.

